
• Learn software testing fundamentals: SDLC, STLC, bug lifecycle.
     SDLC defines the stages/phases involved in developing software to ensure quality and cost-effectiveness.
     Phases:
     Requirement Gathering
     Design
     Implementation (Coding)
     Testing
     Deployment
     Maintenance

     STLC – Software Testing Life Cycle
     STLC is a series of activities performed by testers to ensure software quality.
     Phases:
     Requirement Analysis
     Test Planning
     Test Case Design
     Test Environment Setup
     Test Execution
     Test Closure
 
     Bug/Defect Life Cycle
     The journey of a defect from detection to closure.
     States:
     New → Assigned → Open → Retest → Verified → Closed
     Others: Reopened, Deferred, Rejected, Duplicate, Not a Bug



• Understand different types of testing: Manual vs. Automated, Functional, Non
functional, Regression, Smoke, Sanity. 
    Type	                               Description
    Manual Testing	             Executed manually without tools
    Automated Testing	           Executed using automation tools/scripts
    Functional Testing	         Validates software functions against requirements
    Non-functional               Checks performance, usability, security, etc.
    Regression Testing        	 Ensures updates don't break existing functionality
    Smoke Testing                Basic check to ensure critical features work
    Sanity Testing	             Focused test after a bug fix or code change


• Study test case, test plan, and bug report formats. 
    Field              Description
    Test Case ID    	 Unique ID (e.g., TC_Login_01)
    Module             Area tested (e.g., Login)
    Test Steps	       Actions to perform
    Expected Result    Expected behavior
    Actual Result	     Observed behavior
    Status	           Pass/Fail
    Remarks	           Notes, if any

    Test Plan Format
    Objective
    Scope
    Test Items
    Testing Types
    Test Deliverables
    Schedule
    Resources
    Risk Management

    Bug Report Format
    Field	                         Description
    Bug ID	                  Unique bug identifier
    Title	                    Bug summary
    Steps to Reproduce	      Reproduction steps
    Expected Result         	Expected correct behavior
    Actual Result	            What actually happened
    Severity                 	Critical, Major, Minor
    Priority                	High, Medium, Low
    Environment	              Browser, OS, device, etc.

